# The keymap: every shortcut is a command, looked up by chord and gated by what has focus.
#
# `key` is not a key press — a run posts no input. It asks the same KeymapRules.Dispatch the
# window's key handler asks, with the focus posed, and runs what it names through the same
# registry. So this proves which command a chord belongs to, where it is live, and whether the
# command may run; it cannot prove WPF delivers the key, which only a person at a keyboard can.

tree .
refresh

# --- The window's shortcuts still do what they did ---

key Ctrl+T
assert-tabs 2
key Ctrl+W
assert-tabs 1
key Ctrl+Alt+Right
assert-panes 2
key Ctrl+Shift+W
assert-panes 1

enter Documents
assert-path Documents
key Backspace
assert-not-inside-archive
assert-row Documents
key Alt+Right
assert-path Documents
key Alt+Up
assert-row Documents

key Ctrl+B
assert-flat
key Ctrl+B
assert-not-flat

# --- Where a chord is live is a rule, not an accident of which control saw the key first ---

# Backspace navigates from the list and the tree, and never while somebody is typing.
assert-key Backspace list nav.back
assert-key Backspace other nav.back
assert-key Backspace text none

# The clipboard, Enter, F2 and Del are the list's alone.
assert-key Ctrl+C list edit.copy
assert-key Ctrl+C text none
assert-key Ctrl+C other none
assert-key F2 list file.rename
assert-key F2 other none
assert-key Del list file.delete
assert-key Enter list file.open

# Undo stays out of every text control, the preview's read-only one included.
assert-key Ctrl+Z list edit.undo
assert-key Ctrl+Z text none
assert-key Ctrl+Z readonly none

# A chord no text box uses is live everywhere.
assert-key Ctrl+T text tab.new
assert-key F5 text nav.refresh
assert-key Ctrl+F text search.folder

# --- A command that cannot run says why, and a key cannot route around that ---

assert-command file.rename unavailable Nothing is selected
select notes.txt
assert-command file.rename available
assert-command file.compare-files unavailable exactly two
select notes.txt, report.md
assert-command file.compare-files available
deselect

assert-command edit.undo unavailable nothing to undo
assert-command pane.close unavailable only pane
assert-command tab.reopen available

# Inside an archive, everything that writes by path is off — by menu, by key and by name.
preview-fixture Preview
go Preview
enter sample.zip
assert-inside-archive
select readme.txt
assert-command edit.copy unavailable archive
assert-command edit.cut unavailable archive
assert-command file.new-folder unavailable archive
assert-command file.compress unavailable archive
assert-command file.bookmark unavailable archive
assert-command file.checksum unavailable archive
assert-command file.open-terminal unavailable archive
# Rename and delete stay on in there — they rewrite the container — but rename takes one item.
assert-command file.rename available
assert-command file.delete available
assert-command file.extract-here available
select readme.txt, src
assert-command file.rename unavailable one item at a time
# The chord is still the command's, so it is swallowed rather than falling through to type-ahead.
assert-key Ctrl+Shift+N list file.new-folder
key Ctrl+Shift+N
assert-inside-archive
deselect
up
assert-not-inside-archive

# --- The settings page silences everything about the folders ---

settings general
assert-key Ctrl+T other none
assert-key Backspace other none
assert-key F5 list none
settings close
assert-key Ctrl+T other tab.new

# --- Rebinding ---

assert-gesture view.flat Ctrl+B
bind view.flat Ctrl+K
assert-gesture view.flat Ctrl+K
assert-key Ctrl+B list none
key Ctrl+K
assert-flat
key Ctrl+K
assert-not-flat

# Giving a chord to another command takes it from whoever had it.
bind tab.duplicate Ctrl+T
assert-key Ctrl+T list tab.duplicate
assert-gesture tab.new none

# Taking a shortcut away is a change too, and Reset undoes it.
bind nav.refresh none
assert-key F5 list none
unbind nav.refresh
assert-key F5 list nav.refresh

# --- What is printed follows what is bound ---

# The menu and the tooltips read the keymap in force, so nothing on screen goes on claiming a key
# that no longer does the thing.
select plain.txt
menu files 01-menu-shipped
assert-menu-gesture Rename F2
assert-menu-gesture Delete… Del
assert-menu-gesture Copy as path Ctrl+Shift+C
assert-menu-gesture Folder Ctrl+Shift+N
assert-menu-gesture Bookmark none
assert-tooltip PreviewPaneToggle Ctrl+P

bind file.rename F9
bind file.bookmark Ctrl+D
bind view.preview Ctrl+Shift+V
bind file.new-folder none
menu files 02-menu-rebound
assert-menu-gesture Rename F9
assert-menu-gesture Bookmark Ctrl+D
assert-menu-gesture Folder none
assert-tooltip PreviewPaneToggle Ctrl+Shift+V
assert-key F2 list none
assert-key F9 list file.rename
deselect

unbind
assert-tooltip PreviewPaneToggle Ctrl+P
assert-gesture view.flat Ctrl+B
assert-key Ctrl+T list tab.new
assert-gesture tab.duplicate Ctrl+Shift+K

assert-not-launched
